      },
      "message": "fix(app): pocket recognition refuses an inside-out or open mesh by name\n\npockets_of read \"up\" and \"leans into\" straight off the facet winding, so\nan inside-out cube came back as a closed pocket over its own outline, as\ndeep as the part - and detect_pockets create would cut it to the base.\nIt now asks #387's body-winding verdict first and refuses any body whose\noutside cannot be trusted (inside-out, open, non-manifold, mixed, flat),\nin its own words. Found by the maintainer's review of #512.\n\nPinned by pocket_recognition::an_inside_out_mesh_is_refused_never_read_as_a_pocket\n(fails without the fix: the reversed cube reads as a 10 mm closed pocket)\nand the torn-mesh case in degenerate_input_refuses_cleanly.\n\nFixes #718\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
